WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:50.010 --> 00:01:53.430
<b>The Girl They Called a Devil</b>

3
00:01:53.430 --> 00:01:55.900
[KALIFA]
Those fools braved
Aqua Laguna to get here.

4
00:01:56.540 --> 00:01:58.440
They're determined, if nothing else.

5
00:01:58.440 --> 00:02:01.010
[JABURA]
Humph. Either that,
or they're just lucky.

6
00:02:01.010 --> 00:02:03.750
[LUCCI]
Remember, we have
permission to kill this time.

7
00:02:03.750 --> 00:02:07.750
[KAKU]
But if we kill them, it'll be
over before we have any fun.

8
00:02:07.750 --> 00:02:08.720
[LUFFY]
The drawbridge?

9
00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:12.460
[ZORO]
Yeah. The Franky Family's trying
to get that under control right now.

10
00:02:12.460 --> 00:02:16.740
Once they bring it down, we should be
able to get to the other side, no problem.

11
00:02:16.740 --> 00:02:17.720
[SANJI]
What a pain.

12
00:02:17.720 --> 00:02:21.630
She's right there and
all we can do is wait.

13
00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:31.540
[FRANKY]
Damn it.

14
00:02:31.540 --> 00:02:35.640
What is her deal? She must be
hiding one hell of a secret.

15
00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:40.350
[SPANDAM]
Hey! CP9! Here are your orders!

16
00:02:40.350 --> 00:02:44.360
Kill the intruders, but only engage
them here at the Tower of Law!

17
00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:49.530
My life and my promotion are the
most important things right now.

18
00:02:49.530 --> 00:02:51.400
I have to be careful about this.

19
00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:56.410
If I let all my underlings run off, who's
gonna protect me if something goes wrong?

20
00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:00.590
[SPANDAM]
Stupid pirates!

21
00:03:00.590 --> 00:03:04.700
You may act tough, but you don't know
what you're getting yourselves into!

22
00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:06.460
Open your eyes!

23
00:03:06.460 --> 00:03:07.460
Come on!

24
00:03:07.460 --> 00:03:11.430
You don't think you can
beat all of CP9, do you?

25
00:03:11.430 --> 00:03:13.470
And what about the Gates of Justice?

26
00:03:13.470 --> 00:03:15.540
You don't think you
can open them, do you?

27
00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:19.250
Even then. If things
go wrong, I have this!

28
00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:25.950
The Golden Transponder Snail, giving me
the authority to issue a Buster Call!

29
00:03:25.950 --> 00:03:27.490
[ROBIN]
A Buster Call?

30
00:03:27.490 --> 00:03:30.020
Yes. That's right.

31
00:03:30.020 --> 00:03:33.040
I'm sure you remember its power well.

32
00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:37.950
After all, it did destroy your
homeland 20 years ago.

33
00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:39.880
What was it, "Ohara?"

34
00:03:39.880 --> 00:03:43.580
Hard to recall the name
since it was wiped off the map!

35
00:03:43.580 --> 00:03:45.820
[CHOPPER]
Robin's homeland?

36
00:03:45.820 --> 00:03:48.390
He's pissing me off.

37
00:03:48.390 --> 00:03:49.520
[ROBIN]
There's no place left.

38
00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:52.620
Nowhere for me to go or return to.

39
00:03:53.320 --> 00:03:56.090
[ROBIN]
Anything but that! I'm begging you!

40
00:03:56.090 --> 00:04:00.800
Ooh. Begging for mercy, I like that!

41
00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:01.870
What's wrong?

42
00:04:01.870 --> 00:04:03.100
You don't want me to press this

43
00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:06.470
and annihilate all your little
friends with a Buster Call?

44
00:04:06.470 --> 00:04:08.370
Is that what you're saying?

45
00:04:09.670 --> 00:04:10.940
You're insane.

46
00:04:10.940 --> 00:04:14.450
If you push that button, do you
have any clue what will happen?

47
00:04:14.450 --> 00:04:16.330
Of course I do!

48
00:04:16.330 --> 00:04:18.460
This button will eliminate
any chance your friends

49
00:04:18.460 --> 00:04:21.480
possibly have of
leaving this island alive!

50
00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:23.440
All it takes is one little press.

51
00:04:23.440 --> 00:04:24.960
It couldn't be more simple!

52
00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:28.100
If you think that, you
don't understand a thing!

53
00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:31.030
Are all those old memories
coming back to you now?

54
00:04:31.870 --> 00:04:32.700
Let's see.

55
00:04:32.700 --> 00:04:35.450
Maybe I should press it after all.

56
00:04:35.450 --> 00:04:37.850
It might be fun.

57
00:04:41.490 --> 00:04:43.890
[ROBIN]
This isn't a joke! Stop it!

58
00:04:45.910 --> 00:04:49.840
I'm the one who makes
the demands here, wench.

59
00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:10.490
[ROBIN]
You say Ohara was wiped off the map,
but your map doesn't show you

60
00:05:10.490 --> 00:05:13.000
the lives of the
people who lived there!

61
00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:15.800
Your view of the world is so distant

62
00:05:15.800 --> 00:05:20.870
and so twisted that you've
lost sight of your humanity!

63
00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:33.330
[ROBIN]
There's a limit to how much you can
sacrifice in the name of justice.

64
00:05:33.330 --> 00:05:36.770
A Buster Call is going too far.

65
00:05:38.390 --> 00:05:40.020
You can't use it.

66
00:05:40.020 --> 00:05:41.930
Anything but that.

67
00:05:44.070 --> 00:05:50.040
<b>Ohara
20 Years Ago – West Blue</b>

68
00:05:52.160 --> 00:05:53.800
[BOY]
All right, get her!

69
00:05:53.800 --> 00:05:55.770
Nice throw! Wow!

70
00:05:54.920 --> 00:05:57.460
<b>Nico Robin (8 Years Old)</b>

71
00:05:58.600 --> 00:06:00.770
Yeah! Bullseye!

72
00:06:00.770 --> 00:06:02.670
[BOY & GIRL]
Take that, monster girl!

73
00:06:02.670 --> 00:06:04.840
[BOY]
Gross! You're so creepy!

74
00:06:05.210 --> 00:06:10.580
[BOYS]
Monster! Monster! Monster! Monster!

75
00:06:14.680 --> 00:06:16.620
[BOYS]
The monster girl hit me!

76
00:06:19.960 --> 00:06:20.760
[GIRL]
She's scary!

77
00:06:20.760 --> 00:06:22.300
[BOY]
You'll be sorry!

78
00:06:44.630 --> 00:06:46.200
[MOTHER]
Hey, you!

79
00:06:49.890 --> 00:06:52.870
My kids came home crying because
you hit them on the head!

80
00:06:52.870 --> 00:06:54.920
What are you thinking,
acting like that?

81
00:06:54.920 --> 00:06:57.060
You stay away from them, you hear me?

82
00:06:58.860 --> 00:07:01.860
Don't you have anything
to say for yourself?

83
00:07:02.430 --> 00:07:05.130
You really are a little
monster, aren't you?

84
00:07:06.380 --> 00:07:08.470
Hey! You come back here!

85
00:07:08.470 --> 00:07:11.080
I'm not done talking with you yet!

86
00:07:18.030 --> 00:07:20.640
[GIRL]
Mommy, mommy, what're we
having for dinner tonight?

87
00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:22.140
[MOTHER]
Well, what would you like?

88
00:07:22.140 --> 00:07:25.880
[GIRL]
Um... um...Rice omelet!

89
00:07:27.180 --> 00:07:28.850
[FATHER]
You sure like rice omelets, huh?

90
00:07:28.850 --> 00:07:29.920
[GIRL]
Yep!

91
00:07:30.070 --> 00:07:32.620
[MOTHER]
Then we'll pick up some
eggs on the way home, okay?

92
00:07:32.620 --> 00:07:34.020
[GIRL]
Okay!

93
00:07:42.010 --> 00:07:44.010
[ROBIN]
Sorry I'm home so late.

94
00:07:44.010 --> 00:07:48.880
Hello, is anyone there? Aunt Roji?

95
00:07:59.410 --> 00:08:01.350
[ROBIN]
"To Robin. Today...

96
00:08:02.220 --> 00:08:04.850
[ROJI]
– as you must know, is
my little girl's birthday.

97
00:08:04.850 --> 00:08:09.760
So the family is going out for a special
dinner tonight, just the three of us.

98
00:08:09.760 --> 00:08:13.800
We left some bread out on the table,
so you can eat that for dinner.

99
00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:17.600
Don't be too greedy with the jam.

100
00:08:17.600 --> 00:08:21.200
When you're done eating,
and before we come back,

101
00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:24.310
I want you to do the dishes,
scrub the floors,

102
00:08:24.310 --> 00:08:27.240
take the laundry inside,
and go straight to bed

103
00:08:27.240 --> 00:08:29.650
as soon as you're
finished with your chores.

104
00:08:36.070 --> 00:08:38.470
[GIRL]
Mommy, mommy, what're
we having for dinner tonight?

105
00:08:38.470 --> 00:08:40.840
[MOTHER]
Well, what would you like?

106
00:08:41.740 --> 00:08:45.540
Um... um...Rice omelet!

107
00:08:45.540 --> 00:08:47.380
[FATHER]
You sure like rice omelets, huh?

108
00:08:47.380 --> 00:08:48.480
[GIRL]
Yep!

109
00:08:48.480 --> 00:08:50.420
[MOTHER]
Then we'll pick up some eggs
on the way home, okay?

110
00:08:50.420 --> 00:08:52.750
[GIRL]
Okay!

111
00:09:05.860 --> 00:09:11.780
<b>The Tree of Knowledge
Ohara Library and Archaeological Research Center</b>

112
00:09:11.760 --> 00:09:13.560
[DR. CLOVER]
Oh! Look! Here comes Robin!

113
00:09:14.570 --> 00:09:16.790
Seems she's stopping
by to return a book.

114
00:09:16.790 --> 00:09:19.100
[DR. CLOVER]
Everyone get in place, quick!

115
00:09:23.600 --> 00:09:25.770
[ROBIN]
Hello? Professor Clover?

116
00:09:25.770 --> 00:09:27.870
I finished the book you lent me.

117
00:09:31.740 --> 00:09:36.850
[SCHOLARS]
One... two... Congratulations, Robin!

118
00:09:33.590 --> 00:09:37.260
<b>The Archaeologists of Ohara</b>

119
00:09:37.180 --> 00:09:39.980
[SCHOLARS]
You're amazing, Robin! A real genius!

120
00:09:40.270 --> 00:09:43.500
[SCHOLARS]
We've got a cake for you, by the way!

121
00:09:43.500 --> 00:09:48.630
[DR. CLOVER]
Robin. That doctoral exam you took the other
day, you passed with a perfect score!

122
00:09:48.630 --> 00:09:52.600
From this day forward, you
are an official archaeologist!

123
00:09:52.600 --> 00:09:54.470
And since you're one of us now,

124
00:09:54.470 --> 00:09:58.400
we can all work on our research
together, starting today!

125
00:09:58.970 --> 00:10:01.740
Here, this proves
that you're a scholar.

126
00:10:01.740 --> 00:10:04.010
Wear it with pride!

127
00:10:04.010 --> 00:10:05.310
[SCHOLARS]
It looks great on you, Robin!

128
00:10:05.310 --> 00:10:07.280
[SCHOLARS]
We're so proud!

129
00:10:08.250 --> 00:10:13.430
<b>Professor Clover (Authority on Archaeology)
Ohara Library's Head Librarian</b>

130
00:10:09.180 --> 00:10:13.750
Now listen up, you must understand what
it means to be an Ohara archeologist.

131
00:10:13.750 --> 00:10:14.750
[ROBIN]
Right!

132
00:10:14.750 --> 00:10:16.490
I'm ready to learn!

133
00:10:16.490 --> 00:10:20.530
Our knowledge, in particular,
comes from the past.

134
00:10:20.530 --> 00:10:23.700
And this library, known
as the Tree of Knowledge,

135
00:10:23.700 --> 00:10:27.540
has stood for over 5,000 years,
collecting countless documents

136
00:10:27.540 --> 00:10:30.470
and literature from
every corner of the world.

137
00:10:30.470 --> 00:10:35.680
This is a treasure for all humanity
to share and nourish for future generations.

138
00:10:35.680 --> 00:10:40.190
As the world's largest library,
knowledge is our pride and joy.

139
00:10:40.190 --> 00:10:42.090
Under the branches of this tree,

140
00:10:42.090 --> 00:10:45.660
the finest archeologists from
every sea have gathered!

141
00:10:45.660 --> 00:10:48.630
With this vast wealth of
information at our disposal,

142
00:10:48.630 --> 00:10:52.170
there is no historical
mystery that cannot be solved!

143
00:10:53.170 --> 00:10:55.070
Are you ready to join us?

144
00:10:55.070 --> 00:10:56.660
Yes sir!

145
00:10:56.660 --> 00:11:00.180
In that case, I look forward to
seeing your research take form,

146
00:11:00.180 --> 00:11:03.480
and watching all the contributions
you will make to the world.

147
00:11:03.480 --> 00:11:08.470
Professor, what I'd really like is to find
out what happened in the "Blank Century"!

148
00:11:09.040 --> 00:11:10.040
No! You can't!

149
00:11:10.040 --> 00:11:13.020
I strictly forbid it,
just as I always have!

150
00:11:13.020 --> 00:11:14.460
Huh? I don't get it.

151
00:11:14.460 --> 00:11:18.350
If we want to solve the mysteries of the
world, shouldn't we study the Poneglyphs

152
00:11:18.350 --> 00:11:20.280
to find out what happened back then?

153
00:11:20.620 --> 00:11:21.320
What?

154
00:11:21.320 --> 00:11:23.350
How do you know about all that?

155
00:11:23.350 --> 00:11:26.050
Did you use your powers to
peek on us in the basement?

156
00:11:26.050 --> 00:11:27.200
I just...

157
00:11:28.140 --> 00:11:30.330
Any attempt to decipher
or study the Poneglyphs

158
00:11:30.330 --> 00:11:33.560
is considered a criminal act
by the World Government!

159
00:11:35.270 --> 00:11:37.090
I see.

160
00:11:37.090 --> 00:11:39.220
So that's why you don't tell anybody.

161
00:11:39.220 --> 00:11:42.050
That's why you study them
in the basement at night.

162
00:11:42.050 --> 00:11:45.520
You were spying on us!

163
00:11:45.520 --> 00:11:47.320
So how much do you know?

164
00:11:47.320 --> 00:11:50.490
This is a very serious matter
we're dealing with here!

165
00:11:50.490 --> 00:11:53.260
Explain yourself, Robin!

166
00:11:53.760 --> 00:11:59.770
I know it's bad, but even if I asked nicely,
you still wouldn't let me join you!

167
00:12:00.780 --> 00:12:04.900
That's why I studied so hard
to become an archeologist

168
00:12:04.900 --> 00:12:08.670
because I thought then you would
finally treat me like everyone else.

169
00:12:08.670 --> 00:12:11.070
I just wanted to learn.

170
00:12:12.940 --> 00:12:15.480
Robin.

171
00:12:16.110 --> 00:12:17.080
I know this is hard.

172
00:12:17.660 --> 00:12:19.800
You've studied with all
your heart and deserve

173
00:12:19.800 --> 00:12:23.180
to be called a scholar as
much as anyone else here.

174
00:12:23.180 --> 00:12:26.250
However, you're also still a child.

175
00:12:26.250 --> 00:12:29.610
If word gets out, then every
one of us could be put to death.

176
00:12:29.610 --> 00:12:33.090
Harsh as that sounds, it's
something we're willing to accept.

177
00:12:33.090 --> 00:12:36.200
Since this became the law
of the world 800 years ago,

178
00:12:36.200 --> 00:12:41.600
countless scholars have lost their lives,
as many as there are stars in the sky!

179
00:12:41.600 --> 00:12:44.810
But we can't stop now,
and I'll tell you why.

180
00:12:44.810 --> 00:12:47.770
Of all the scholars who ever tried
to decipher the ancient texts,

181
00:12:47.770 --> 00:12:51.410
we of Ohara are the only ones
who have met with any success.

182
00:12:52.360 --> 00:12:55.670
For us, there is no turning back.

183
00:12:55.670 --> 00:13:00.010
I swear on the Tree of Knowledge, if you
ever come close to the basement again,

184
00:13:00.010 --> 00:13:04.280
you will be forbidden from entering the
library or conducting research with us!

185
00:13:04.280 --> 00:13:06.010
You understand?

186
00:13:09.620 --> 00:13:11.420
[SCHOLARS]
Robin!

187
00:13:11.420 --> 00:13:15.360
[SCHOLARS]
I hate to say this, especially now,
but she's just like her mom.

188
00:13:15.360 --> 00:13:19.330
It's only a matter of time before
she uncovers that secret, too.

189
00:13:20.000 --> 00:13:24.230
[DR. CLOVER]
Her mother Olvia was only captured
by Marines a few days ago.

190
00:13:24.230 --> 00:13:27.370
But it's already clear
what fate she'll suffer.

191
00:13:28.500 --> 00:13:31.540
<b>The Following Day</b>

192
00:14:17.340 --> 00:14:19.420
[SAUL]
Wa... water.

193
00:14:21.760 --> 00:14:23.220
[ROBIN]
Wawater?

194
00:14:32.230 --> 00:14:34.310
[SAUL]
Perfect!

195
00:14:38.270 --> 00:14:42.440
<b>Saul, a Castaway Giant</b>

196
00:14:42.490 --> 00:14:45.200
Guess I'm still alive after all.

197
00:14:45.660 --> 00:14:48.950
I just wonder if she's okay, too.

198
00:14:50.120 --> 00:14:54.190
Anyhow, thank you for
your help, but I gotta ask...

199
00:14:54.840 --> 00:14:57.680
is there a town or village
somewhere 'round here?

200
00:14:58.850 --> 00:15:01.090
That's a shame.

201
00:15:01.890 --> 00:15:07.430
I 'spose beggars can't be choosers,
but a deserted island woulda been nice, y'know?

202
00:15:14.730 --> 00:15:18.300
You can stare all you want,
but ain't nothing gonna happen.

203
00:15:18.560 --> 00:15:22.300
As you can see, I hurt
my leg, so I'm stayin' put.

204
00:15:22.300 --> 00:15:24.530
'Least for the time bein'.

205
00:15:24.530 --> 00:15:29.040
After I feel a little better, I'll build
a raft or somethin' to get me outta here.

206
00:15:30.460 --> 00:15:33.370
This your first time
seeing a giant, Missy?

207
00:15:33.370 --> 00:15:34.710
[ROBIN]
Yeah.

208
00:15:34.710 --> 00:15:36.430
I'll tell you one thing,

209
00:15:36.430 --> 00:15:40.600
I may be big as those guys from
Elbaf, but I sure ain't as mean.

210
00:15:40.600 --> 00:15:44.640
Just as sure as there's war-like
giants, there's peaceful ones, too.

211
00:15:44.640 --> 00:15:46.510
Huh.

212
00:15:47.110 --> 00:15:50.670
[SAUL]
I know this is a long shot,
but I gotta ask anyway.

213
00:15:50.670 --> 00:15:53.510
When you get home, you
think maybe you could...uh...

214
00:15:53.510 --> 00:15:56.410
not tell anyone that a giant
washed up on the beach?

215
00:15:56.410 --> 00:15:58.210
Okay, sure.

216
00:15:58.210 --> 00:16:00.350
Well, that was too easy.

217
00:16:00.350 --> 00:16:02.380
Of course you're gonna tell people.

218
00:16:02.380 --> 00:16:04.620
I said I wouldn't.

219
00:16:08.290 --> 00:16:10.020
Yeah, you're tellin' a fib.

220
00:16:10.020 --> 00:16:14.130
Ain't no way a kid can
keep a secret this big!

221
00:16:14.130 --> 00:16:15.540
Don't worry about it.

222
00:16:15.540 --> 00:16:17.980
I'm not really interested in you.

223
00:16:23.260 --> 00:16:24.960
Dereshishishi. Dereshishishi.

224
00:16:24.960 --> 00:16:29.790
Dereshishishi. Dereshishishi.
Dereshishishi. Dereshishishi.

225
00:16:33.390 --> 00:16:36.840
"Dereshi"? What does that mean?

226
00:16:36.840 --> 00:16:38.340
It don't mean a darn thing!

227
00:16:38.340 --> 00:16:40.480
I'm just laughing!

228
00:16:42.410 --> 00:16:44.450
That's the way you laugh?

229
00:16:44.450 --> 00:16:47.180
[SAUL]
You sure are a funny little girl!

230
00:16:51.670 --> 00:16:53.940
You're the funny one!

231
00:16:56.210 --> 00:16:57.310
I gotta admit,

232
00:16:57.660 --> 00:17:00.610
all my life people been
tellin' me my laugh is silly.

233
00:17:00.610 --> 00:17:04.240
But you, you're pretty
cute when you laugh!

234
00:17:04.240 --> 00:17:08.750
You should do it more
often, I say! Dereshishishi.

235
00:17:08.750 --> 00:17:11.280
Anyhow, I go by the name of Saul.

236
00:17:11.280 --> 00:17:15.220
Jaguar D. Saul, if you like.

237
00:17:15.220 --> 00:17:16.320
"D"?

238
00:17:16.320 --> 00:17:17.490
Yeah.

239
00:17:17.490 --> 00:17:20.100
I don't much know what it
means but from what I hear,

240
00:17:20.100 --> 00:17:23.100
everyone in my family has
it for their middle name.

241
00:17:23.100 --> 00:17:25.100
Anyways, what about you?

242
00:17:25.100 --> 00:17:26.310
[ROBIN]
My name's Robin.

243
00:17:26.310 --> 00:17:27.580
I see.

244
00:17:27.580 --> 00:17:31.550
Well, truth is, Robin, some guys
are chasing me down right now.

245
00:17:31.550 --> 00:17:34.720
So, uh, if someone
finds me, I'm in trouble.

246
00:17:34.720 --> 00:17:36.720
[ROBIN]
I said I wouldn't tell!

247
00:17:37.660 --> 00:17:41.160
<b>Three Days After the Giant Drifted Ashore</b>

248
00:17:47.350 --> 00:17:48.290
Good!

249
00:17:49.480 --> 00:17:50.910
[ROBIN]
Here's another one.

250
00:17:53.790 --> 00:17:57.530
Mighty kind of you, Robin, but
you go ahead and take this one.

251
00:17:57.530 --> 00:18:00.430
My stomach's pretty full as-is.

252
00:18:00.430 --> 00:18:03.900
As you can see, I caught
a real whopper last night.

253
00:18:06.090 --> 00:18:09.460
Well, I better get back
to work on that raft.

254
00:18:09.460 --> 00:18:12.070
Should be done
pretty soon at this rate.

255
00:18:16.620 --> 00:18:20.880
I don't mean to pry, but it seems like you
have an awful lot of time on your hands.

256
00:18:20.880 --> 00:18:25.030
Not that I don't like your company,
but you've been sticking with me for days now.

257
00:18:25.030 --> 00:18:28.430
Ain't your parents and
friends gonna get suspicious?

258
00:18:28.430 --> 00:18:30.940
I don't have any parents.

259
00:18:30.940 --> 00:18:34.980
Actually, I do have a mom, but she set sail
for work years ago and never came back.

260
00:18:34.980 --> 00:18:36.640
I don't even remember her face.

261
00:18:37.090 --> 00:18:39.690
I'm sort-of-friends with the
archaeologists around here,

262
00:18:39.690 --> 00:18:43.790
but they won't let me join in on their
research, so I don't know anymore.

263
00:18:43.790 --> 00:18:47.470
The other kids say I'm creepy,
so even if I wanted to play with them,

264
00:18:47.470 --> 00:18:51.210
I don't think that they'd let me.

265
00:18:51.210 --> 00:18:54.710
[SAUL]
Ah, so you have
Devil Fruit powers, huh?

266
00:18:55.250 --> 00:18:56.450
You aren't scared of me?

267
00:18:56.450 --> 00:18:59.850
I used to sail all over the
Grand Line back in the day.

268
00:18:59.850 --> 00:19:03.620
I've seen plenty of folks with
powers tons scarier than yours.

269
00:19:03.620 --> 00:19:06.890
To be honest, I'm kinda jealous
of your little arm thing.

270
00:19:06.890 --> 00:19:14.970
It looks pretty handy!
Dereshishishi. Dereshishishi.

271
00:19:15.470 --> 00:19:17.370
That laugh of yours is really weird!

272
00:19:17.770 --> 00:19:18.470
Dereshishishi.

273
00:19:18.470 --> 00:19:20.570
It don't matter if your laugh's weird,

274
00:19:21.810 --> 00:19:24.240
all that really matters,
is when you laugh,

275
00:19:24.240 --> 00:19:27.100
all of a sudden,
your problems disappear!

276
00:19:27.100 --> 00:19:27.800
[ROBIN]
Why?

277
00:19:27.800 --> 00:19:28.900
[SAUL]
What d'you mean "why?"

278
00:19:29.570 --> 00:19:32.910
Everyone knows you laugh
when you're having fun, right?

279
00:19:32.910 --> 00:19:35.510
So if you're not having fun,
all you need to do is laugh

280
00:19:35.510 --> 00:19:38.010
and everything'll work out just fine!

281
00:19:38.010 --> 00:19:41.420
You're just a kid, but it seems
like you're having a tough time.

282
00:19:41.420 --> 00:19:43.380
When you're feelin' down, just laugh.

283
00:19:43.380 --> 00:19:46.020
There ain't nothin'
a good laugh can't fix.

284
00:19:46.020 --> 00:19:48.890
It seems awfully silly
to laugh when you're sad.

285
00:19:48.890 --> 00:19:50.610
[SAUL]
Don't knock it tell you try it!

286
00:19:50.610 --> 00:19:53.550
Here. "Dereshishi!"

287
00:19:53.550 --> 00:19:57.350
Do it just like that and I bet
you'll feel better in a flash!

288
00:20:01.020 --> 00:20:02.460
Deresh!

289
00:20:02.460 --> 00:20:06.350
[SAUL]
Not bad! Now, with more gusto!

290
00:20:06.350 --> 00:20:09.320
[ROBIN]
Dereshishishishi!

291
00:20:12.740 --> 00:20:14.850
Dereshishishi!

292
00:20:14.850 --> 00:20:17.050
Now that's more like it!

293
00:20:21.420 --> 00:20:23.320
[MARINE (OVER SNAIL)]
This is Navy Headquarters here.

294
00:20:23.320 --> 00:20:26.020
Once again, we're hoping we
could speak to Chief Spandine.

295
00:20:26.020 --> 00:20:27.920
[AGENT]
You heard 'em, Chief. What now?

296
00:20:27.920 --> 00:20:28.890
[SPANDINE]
Ignore them.

297
00:20:28.890 --> 00:20:31.380
They probably just
want a status report.

298
00:20:31.170 --> 00:20:34.710
<b>Somewhere in the West Blue</b>

299
00:20:31.380 --> 00:20:33.320
We'll contact them
when we see the shore.

300
00:20:33.320 --> 00:20:35.200
That's good enough.

301
00:20:34.760 --> 00:20:41.890
<b>Spandine, CP9 Chief
(20 Years Ago)</b>

302
00:20:35.200 --> 00:20:38.000
[SPANDINE]
Ohara, Opera, O-whatever, who cares?

303
00:20:38.000 --> 00:20:39.240
Why are they wasting my time,

304
00:20:39.240 --> 00:20:42.170
making me trek all the way out
here to the West Blue, huh?

305
00:20:42.170 --> 00:20:46.160
Let's get this over with, then
get the hell outta this dump.

306
00:20:47.390 --> 00:20:52.150
<b>The Following Day, Four Days After the Giant Drifted Ashore</b>

307
00:21:07.200 --> 00:21:08.070
[MAN]
Hey, is it true?

308
00:21:08.070 --> 00:21:09.770
We've got a Navy ship on the island?

309
00:21:09.770 --> 00:21:10.440
What?

310
00:21:10.440 --> 00:21:11.840
I haven't heard about that!

311
00:21:11.840 --> 00:21:13.740
[MAN]
Yeah, it must've
anchored here over night.

312
00:21:13.740 --> 00:21:15.310
[MAN]
Why would the Navy come here?

313
00:21:15.310 --> 00:21:16.080
I know.

314
00:21:16.080 --> 00:21:17.380
We're pretty remote.

315
00:21:17.380 --> 00:21:19.210
[MAN]
Weird thing is, when people
went to look at the boat,

316
00:21:19.210 --> 00:21:21.330
they didn't see any marines there.

317
00:21:21.330 --> 00:21:22.850
[MAN]
Wow, that is weird.

318
00:21:22.850 --> 00:21:24.160
[MAN]
It was like a ghost ship.

319
00:21:24.160 --> 00:21:26.090
Not a single person to be found.

320
00:21:26.090 --> 00:21:28.360
[MAN]
C'mon, now you're just fooling with us.

321
00:21:28.360 --> 00:21:29.600
[SCHOLARS]
Professor!

322
00:21:29.600 --> 00:21:31.240
Professor Clover!

323
00:21:32.690 --> 00:21:34.320
Hm?

324
00:21:34.320 --> 00:21:36.430
[DR. CLOVER]
My goodness, did something happen?

325
00:21:36.430 --> 00:21:39.260
[SCHOLARS]
I hope it's nothing to worry
about, but I just heard that

326
00:21:39.260 --> 00:21:41.580
there's a huge navy ship
anchored at the seashore.

327
00:21:41.580 --> 00:21:42.610
We should take precautions.

328
00:21:42.610 --> 00:21:44.900
It might be an investigation.

329
00:21:44.900 --> 00:21:47.230
[DR. CLOVER]
Better let the other scholars know.

330
00:21:50.190 --> 00:21:52.210
[SAUL]
The raft is done!

331
00:21:52.210 --> 00:21:53.610
All right!

332
00:21:58.910 --> 00:22:01.150
[ROBIN]
So you're leaving already?

333
00:22:01.150 --> 00:22:03.020
Now what's with that face?

334
00:22:03.020 --> 00:22:06.150
You put those puppy dog
eyes away, little missy!

335
00:22:07.630 --> 00:22:08.800
Actually.

336
00:22:08.800 --> 00:22:11.270
I s'pose my raft could use a flag, huh?

337
00:22:11.270 --> 00:22:14.510
Guess I'll just have to
stay a little bit longer!

338
00:22:21.180 --> 00:22:22.210
[SAUL]
I'll be darned.

339
00:22:22.210 --> 00:22:24.880
So you're looking to
set out to sea, too, huh?

340
00:22:24.880 --> 00:22:25.580
[ROBIN]
Mm-hm.

341
00:22:25.580 --> 00:22:27.480
My mom's been away from home for years

342
00:22:28.920 --> 00:22:31.420
thanks to all her big
archeological research.

343
00:22:31.420 --> 00:22:34.230
But whenever she finally
comes back to the island,

344
00:22:34.230 --> 00:22:37.320
I'm gonna ask her to take
me along on her next trip.

345
00:22:37.320 --> 00:22:39.810
That's why I've been studying so hard.

346
00:22:39.810 --> 00:22:42.280
I got my archaeology
doctorate just like her.

347
00:22:42.280 --> 00:22:44.040
You got a doctorate?

348
00:22:44.040 --> 00:22:46.330
A tiny little girlie like you?

349
00:22:46.330 --> 00:22:47.800
Mm-hm!

350
00:22:48.130 --> 00:22:49.750
[SAUL]
But hold on a sec.

351
00:22:49.750 --> 00:22:53.730
Didn't you tell me you don't even
remember what your mom's face looks like?

352
00:22:53.730 --> 00:22:56.780
[ROBIN]
Yeah, but she's still my mom.

353
00:22:56.780 --> 00:22:58.980
I wanna see her.

354
00:23:01.280 --> 00:23:03.020
[ROBIN]
Hey, Saul.

355
00:23:03.020 --> 00:23:03.710
[SAUL]
Huh?

356
00:23:03.710 --> 00:23:05.480
Did you know that
our world has a period

357
00:23:05.480 --> 00:23:08.010
of 100 years that nobody
knows anything about?

358
00:23:08.010 --> 00:23:09.250
Uh-huh.

359
00:23:09.250 --> 00:23:12.390
I believe folks call that the
"Blank Century" don't they?

360
00:23:12.390 --> 00:23:13.690
I'm curious about it myself,

361
00:23:13.690 --> 00:23:17.160
but the government says it's
illegal for anyone to look into.

362
00:23:17.160 --> 00:23:18.460
[ROBIN]
That's right.

363
00:23:18.460 --> 00:23:22.880
But I heard my mom is traveling all over
the world investigating it in secret.

364
00:23:22.880 --> 00:23:26.750
But don't tell anyone, I don't
want her to get in trouble.

365
00:23:26.750 --> 00:23:27.960
[SAUL]
What?

366
00:23:27.960 --> 00:23:30.160
Are you telling me that your
mom's going around looking

367
00:23:30.160 --> 00:23:33.970
for them ancient stone tablet
things they call Poneglyphs?

368
00:23:33.970 --> 00:23:35.970
You've heard about Poneglyphs?

369
00:23:35.970 --> 00:23:38.030
Yeah, but that ain't
the point here, okay?

370
00:23:38.030 --> 00:23:39.230
You can't go around talking about

371
00:23:39.230 --> 00:23:41.710
this kinda stuff in front of
other folks outta the blue!

372
00:23:41.710 --> 00:23:43.750
And if yer mamma's out
there looking for them,

373
00:23:44.500 --> 00:23:46.800
you especially gotta be...

374
00:23:47.740 --> 00:23:48.670
Huh?

375
00:23:48.670 --> 00:23:49.670
Is something wrong?

376
00:23:49.670 --> 00:23:53.860
[SAUL]
Robin, do you happen to
know your mother's name?

377
00:23:53.860 --> 00:23:58.830
It's Olvia. Nico Olvia.

378
00:24:06.120 --> 00:24:07.450
You okay?

379
00:24:08.330 --> 00:24:12.440
[SAUL]
Robin is Olvia's daughter!

380
00:24:12.440 --> 00:24:17.470
Wait, so does that mean...I've
been on Ohara all this time?

381
00:24:17.470 --> 00:24:18.550
[ROBIN]
Mm-hm.

382
00:24:18.550 --> 00:24:22.180
That's terrible! Oh no!

383
00:24:22.180 --> 00:24:26.850
Why did I end up in
Ohara of all places?

384
00:24:26.850 --> 00:24:29.390
This is no time to be
sitting around, Saul! Robin!

385
00:24:29.390 --> 00:24:30.720
[ROBIN]
Yes?

386
00:24:30.720 --> 00:24:34.010
[SAUL]
This may come as a shock, but you
gotta listen to me and listen good!

387
00:24:34.010 --> 00:24:37.550
Navy battleships are on
their way to Ohara right now.

388
00:24:37.550 --> 00:24:39.350
They may even be here already!

389
00:24:39.350 --> 00:24:41.350
[ROBIN]
The Navy? Why?

390
00:24:41.350 --> 00:24:44.750
[SAUL]
They're gonna wipe out every
last scholar on the island!

391
00:24:45.810 --> 00:24:48.020
That can't be. No.

392
00:24:48.750 --> 00:24:50.750
So listen, whatever you do.

393
00:24:50.750 --> 00:24:51.450
[ROBIN]
You're lying.

394
00:24:51.450 --> 00:24:53.350
You can't let those government
guys know you're a scholar.

395
00:24:54.020 --> 00:24:54.720
You're lying!

396
00:24:54.720 --> 00:24:56.220
You gotta promise me that, okay?

397
00:24:56.220 --> 00:24:57.790
Stop lying to me!

398
00:24:57.790 --> 00:25:01.860
It's true, I swear... I wouldn't
joke about something this serious!

399
00:25:01.860 --> 00:25:05.300
Get to town as quick as you can and
see if anything strange is going on.

400
00:25:05.300 --> 00:25:08.970
I know it sounds crazy, but
your mom might be there, too!

401
00:25:16.490 --> 00:25:19.040
<b>Nico Olvia
Archaeologist</b>

402
00:25:17.100 --> 00:25:19.270
[NICO OLIVIA]
It's been a while, hasn't it?

403
00:25:19.270 --> 00:25:20.130
[SCHOLARS]
It's Olvia.

404
00:25:20.130 --> 00:25:21.270
You came back.

405
00:25:21.270 --> 00:25:23.470
We'd heard news that you'd
been captured by the Navy!

406
00:25:23.470 --> 00:25:26.370
[SCHOLARS]
Don't tell me you
came back on their ship!

407
00:25:33.310 --> 00:25:38.350
[NICO OLIVIA]
I hate to have to tell you this as soon
I return, but the news you heard is true.

408
00:25:38.350 --> 00:25:40.120
[DR. CLOVER]
It's not your fault...we
knew the government

409
00:25:40.120 --> 00:25:42.430
would set its sights
on Ohara eventually.

410
00:25:42.430 --> 00:25:44.530
I'm not sure how much you know,

411
00:25:44.530 --> 00:25:47.200
but the Poneglyph search
team that set off six years ago

412
00:25:47.200 --> 00:25:49.420
was annihilated by the Marines.

413
00:25:49.420 --> 00:25:51.460
33 researchers were killed.

414
00:25:51.460 --> 00:25:54.930
I was the... the only survivor.

415
00:25:54.930 --> 00:25:57.100
Fortunately, I was only captured,

416
00:25:57.100 --> 00:25:59.670
but I overheard the Marines
talking after they had rummaged

417
00:25:59.670 --> 00:26:01.470
through the search team's belongings.

418
00:26:01.470 --> 00:26:05.170
They soon realized that
we all came from Ohara.

419
00:26:05.740 --> 00:26:11.310
I won't make any excuses, all of you are
in danger because of my carelessness.

420
00:26:11.310 --> 00:26:14.370
Stop it! Thinking like
that won't do any good!

421
00:26:14.370 --> 00:26:18.520
Those who set out to sea and those who
stayed behind are all part of the same team!

422
00:26:18.520 --> 00:26:21.720
After what happened, if anyone
should apologize, it's us.

423
00:26:22.590 --> 00:26:25.690
We know how much you've suffered.

424
00:26:26.660 --> 00:26:28.100
Professor.

425
00:26:28.100 --> 00:26:32.540
For years now, the World Government has
seen Ohara as a threat to their rule.

426
00:26:32.540 --> 00:26:35.470
But all we can do is believe
in the truth of history,

427
00:26:35.470 --> 00:26:38.100
and its value to
all generations to come.

428
00:26:38.100 --> 00:26:41.440
Be that as it may, they've put us
in quite a compromising position.

429
00:26:41.440 --> 00:26:43.980
I just don't know how we're
going to get out of this one.

430
00:26:43.980 --> 00:26:45.920
[NICO OLIVIA]
I admit, it doesn't look good,

431
00:26:45.920 --> 00:26:48.890
but we're fortunate to have discovered
this information when we did.

432
00:26:48.890 --> 00:26:52.160
We know that the government is hunting
down all the scholars on the island.

433
00:26:52.160 --> 00:26:56.550
So before they make it to the library,
we have to escape from Ohara!

434
00:26:56.550 --> 00:26:58.010
[DR. CLOVER]
You have a point.

435
00:26:58.010 --> 00:27:00.450
This time, I have a
feeling we won't be able

436
00:27:00.450 --> 00:27:03.620
to slip past their investigation
like we have before.

437
00:27:03.620 --> 00:27:07.390
And if they're committed to killing us,
they won't listen to reason, either.

438
00:27:07.390 --> 00:27:09.090
Then hurry up and run!

439
00:27:09.090 --> 00:27:10.490
[DR. CLOVER]
I'm sorry, Olvia.

440
00:27:10.490 --> 00:27:15.370
I can't let myself escape and leave one
of mankind's greatest treasures behind.

441
00:27:15.370 --> 00:27:17.010
You should know that.

442
00:27:17.010 --> 00:27:19.180
Everyone else here feels the same way.

443
00:27:19.180 --> 00:27:20.080
Yeah.

444
00:27:20.080 --> 00:27:21.880
Are you sure?

445
00:27:21.880 --> 00:27:24.520
We still don't know what the government's
gonna do when they get here.

446
00:27:24.520 --> 00:27:28.160
But we do know, if we run, we can't
protect all this precious knowledge.

447
00:27:28.160 --> 00:27:30.190
We're not planning on dying here.

448
00:27:30.450 --> 00:27:31.360
Don't worry.

449
00:27:31.360 --> 00:27:33.030
[DR. CLOVER]
More importantly.

450
00:27:33.030 --> 00:27:36.820
I know you have something
else weighing on your mind.

451
00:27:36.820 --> 00:27:37.520
I can't.

452
00:27:37.520 --> 00:27:39.970
It's too late for that.

453
00:27:39.970 --> 00:27:41.800
[SCHOLARS]
Make up your mind, Olvia!

454
00:27:42.090 --> 00:27:44.360
Are you going to
board this ship or not?

455
00:27:44.360 --> 00:27:45.640
[SCHOLARS]
If you want to stay with your daughter,

456
00:27:45.640 --> 00:27:48.630
we'll settle your husband's
unfinished business for you.

457
00:27:48.630 --> 00:27:51.710
No, I'm not turning back.

458
00:27:51.710 --> 00:27:53.750
I'm a scholar of Ohara.

459
00:27:53.750 --> 00:27:58.680
It's my duty to carry out the will
of those who came before me!

460
00:27:58.680 --> 00:28:00.320
Forgive me Robin.

461
00:28:00.320 --> 00:28:04.390
I swear I'll solve these mysteries
and come back to you some day.

462
00:28:09.000 --> 00:28:11.000
[ROBIN]
Where's my mommy?

463
00:28:11.800 --> 00:28:13.540
Where'd she go?

464
00:28:13.540 --> 00:28:15.610
[UNCLE]
Your mom had to go
out to sea for her job.

465
00:28:15.610 --> 00:28:18.970
You'll be staying here with
us for a little while, okay?

466
00:28:18.970 --> 00:28:19.840
[ROJI]
That's enough!

467
00:28:19.840 --> 00:28:21.010
If you don't shut up, I'll hit you!

468
00:28:21.010 --> 00:28:23.110
[UNCLE]
Honey stop it, she's only two!

469
00:28:23.110 --> 00:28:25.040
[ROJI]
And so is our daughter!

470
00:28:25.040 --> 00:28:27.980
Listen, I don't care if she's your
sister's child, she's a burden!

471
00:28:27.980 --> 00:28:30.020
This was a mistake!

472
00:28:35.080 --> 00:28:37.410
[DR. CLOVER]
Who's there? What're you doing here?

473
00:28:39.480 --> 00:28:42.950
Uh, I was...I...I mean, I just...

474
00:28:45.630 --> 00:28:47.270
I'm so sorry!

475
00:28:49.470 --> 00:28:52.770
[DR. CLOVER]
If you want to read a book,
all you have to do is ask, all right?

476
00:28:52.770 --> 00:28:55.740
But I can't, 'cause
I don't have any money.

477
00:28:55.740 --> 00:29:00.310
[DR. CLOVER]
Well, then looks like you're in luck,
because you can read everything here for free.

478
00:29:00.310 --> 00:29:01.010
[ROBIN]
For free?

479
00:29:01.010 --> 00:29:03.880
[DR. CLOVER]
Uh-huh! After all, this library
is the best in the world!

480
00:29:04.590 --> 00:29:05.560
[ROBIN]
Is it really?

481
00:29:05.560 --> 00:29:09.700
[DR. CLOVER]
It sure is! Let's see, unless I'm
mistaken, you're Olvia's daughter.

482
00:29:09.700 --> 00:29:12.630
You like to read books?

483
00:29:15.300 --> 00:29:18.340
She looks just like you did
when you were that age.

484
00:29:18.340 --> 00:29:22.110
And I'm proud to say she's
every bit as clever, too.

485
00:29:22.110 --> 00:29:25.350
If she's safe, that's enough.

486
00:29:25.350 --> 00:29:29.270
When I decided to join you,
I severed all bonds with her.

487
00:29:29.270 --> 00:29:32.640
I can't let her become
the daughter of a criminal.

488
00:29:33.510 --> 00:29:34.460
[SCHOLARS]
Bad news!

489
00:29:34.460 --> 00:29:36.900
Another ship came with
the World Government's flag!

490
00:29:36.900 --> 00:29:38.770
One of their high-ranked
officials coming

491
00:29:38.770 --> 00:29:40.340
all the way here to the West Blue?

492
00:29:40.340 --> 00:29:45.910
My goodness. It seems this
is quite serious indeed!

493
00:29:47.180 --> 00:29:48.450
All right everyone, listen.

494
00:29:48.450 --> 00:29:52.390
From now on, you and I are neither
colleagues nor acquaintances.

495
00:29:53.700 --> 00:29:56.540
You have to stick to
that no matter what.

496
00:29:56.540 --> 00:29:57.510
Farewell!

497
00:29:57.510 --> 00:30:00.430
[DR. CLOVER]
Olvia, wait! What are
you're going to do?

498
00:30:00.190 --> 00:30:04.160
<b>Ohara Coastline</b>

499
00:30:00.430 --> 00:30:03.570
[SPANDINE]
All right, tell HQ we've arrived.

500
00:30:04.230 --> 00:30:07.360
Let's move it!
I wanna get this over with!

501
00:30:08.350 --> 00:30:10.050
[SPANDINE]
What a pain.

502
00:30:11.070 --> 00:30:14.340
They better give me a promotion
when this crap is over.

503
00:30:14.340 --> 00:30:18.440
Hey! I want you to hunt down every
scholar on the island and restrain them.

504
00:30:18.440 --> 00:30:19.630
[OFFICIALS]
Yes sir!

505
00:30:19.630 --> 00:30:20.560
What's going on?

506
00:30:20.560 --> 00:30:22.830
[MAN]
Some woman is running
around with a gun!

507
00:30:41.460 --> 00:30:46.370
This is an awful mess!
I'm sorry, Robin!

508
00:30:46.740 --> 00:30:50.120
<b>Somewhere in the West Blue</b>

509
00:30:47.080 --> 00:30:48.120
[MARINE]
Vice Admiral Kuzan!

510
00:30:48.120 --> 00:30:49.720
[KUZAN]
Huh? What is it?

511
00:30:49.720 --> 00:30:53.990
[MARINE]
We've been informed that CP9's Chief,
Spandine, has arrived in Ohara.

512
00:30:53.990 --> 00:30:55.190
[KUZAN]
So what?

513
00:30:55.190 --> 00:30:59.530
Did you really have to wake
me up just to tell me that?

514
00:30:57.590 --> 00:31:01.050
<b>Vice Admiral Kuzan, Marine Headquarters
(Later to Become Admiral Aokiji)</b>

515
00:30:59.530 --> 00:31:01.010
[MARINE]
I'm sorry, sir!
